  "narrative": {
    "intro": "V3GATE has $977M in contract obligations for FY2026 to date. V3GATE has 667 awards this fiscal year, with an average award size of $1.5M, and obligations are up 18.9% year over year. V3GATE received progressively larger annual obligations from FY21 through FY26: $371M in FY21, $387M in FY22, $648M in FY23, $711M in FY24, $822M in FY25, and $977M in FY26. The Department of Veterans Affairs is the largest buyer, obligating $602M this year. The next largest buying agencies are the Department of State with $67.8M, the Department of Justice with $66.4M, and the Department of Homeland Security with $62.3M. Other buying agencies include the Department of Defense with $32.7M, the Department of Transportation with $27.4M, and the Department of Energy with $23.2M. The dominant market by NAICS is Other Computer Related Services at $972M, followed by Custom Computer Programming Services at $2.8M and Software Publishers at $736K.",
    "sections": [
